## Context
Parent: 1229. An author-called skill that runs only in the harness repo
(outside it, it refuses with one line) and is never scheduled or triggered at
session start. It runs the 1234 lint script for the mechanical checks and itself covers
what that script cannot:
contradiction within or between skills and rules, and a skill presuming or
paraphrasing another skill's responsibility.

Reference material moves under `skills/harness-doctor/references/`:
- the skill-writing guide, now `rules/authoring-skills.md`;
- the author's checklist (see 1229);
- the evidence base in `docs/2026-04-03-harness-best-practices-research.md`
  and `docs/Forsythe-2026-10principles.md`, as pointers.

Trade-off to settle in the PR: `rules/authoring-skills.md` loads on every
skill edit through its `paths:` frontmatter, and two tests cite it. Moving
it wholesale removes that edit-time prompt. Default: leave a path-scoped stub
of a few lines naming the enforced bullets and pointing to the reference.

Runtime diagnostics: the doctor knows and runs the diagnostics each runtime
ships, and reads their output as evidence beside its own pass. Claude Code:
`/skill-doctor` report, `claude plugin eval`, `/doctor`. Codex and Pi:
inventory what they ship (`docs/2026-09-16-runtime-capability-survey.md` is
the starting point) and record the absence where there is none.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Skill passes the 1234 script itself: under 150 lines, scripts in `scripts/`
- [ ] Description pass first; full bodies read only for overlapping pairs
- [ ] Each finding names both files and the conflicting lines; findings above
      the severity floor become tickets, the rest are reported
- [ ] Runtime diagnostics inventoried per runtime and invoked where present;
      an unavailable diagnostic is reported as unavailable, not as clean
- [ ] Reference material moved; `authoring-skills.md` stub or move decided
      and the tests that cite it updated
- [ ] Retirement clause in the skill: three consecutive runs with no finding
      above the floor and the author is asked whether to delete it
